	"notes": "This is GitLab's own project browser, and it uses the two-column app shape: a thin strip of navigation on the left, one wide list of projects on the right. On a phone that strip is hidden and slides in from off-screen when the hamburger icon is tapped, rather than always sitting on the page. The surprising part shows up only in the scan, not in the picture: on a very wide screen the list does not actually get any wider, it stays capped at about 1272 pixels and the leftover room just becomes blank margin, so a big monitor shows the same amount of information with more silence around it. The list itself is plain stacked rows the whole time — it never turns into a grid of cards, no matter how wide the window gets.",
